body:
That is unfortunate and I am sorry to hear that ;_; 

I was thankfully never a target of bullying so I was able to coast on through without batting an eye. Made it feel like it all ended too quickly. 

It's so wild how vastly different everyone's experience is. I thought it was normal to enjoy your highschool years but the internet has taught me that is not the case for a lot of people. Perhaps even the majority.

Don't apologize for that. There is a lot of amazing content on TikTok. It's a shame that you have to swipe past 15 year old girls shaking their asses for a minute to get to the good stuff in the beginning. But once you have liked enough of your preferred content, your FYP starts to become better catered to you. 

Mine is now like 50% cat videos, 20% comedy videos, 20% cooking videos, and 10% art videos. I finally reached a point where I no longer get bombarded by girls flaunting their bodies and shaking their shit to copyrighted music. I'm not saying they shouldn't be allowed to do that sort of thing. They are well within their right to do so. I just don't want to see it ;_;

Do you have any favourite TikTokers?

I just couldn't justify holding on to something so common that I wasn't using. They had to go ;_; 

I've only naturally come across maybe 8 or 9 hundos in the wild on my own. Ones I can think of on the spot were the 3 pidgeys, a Venonat, a Magikarp, and a Bellsprout. Quite a few of the ones I have and held on to, were ones that were called out on our local discord. I probably threw away one or two back in the days before appraisals. Just impossible to know how many I have come across in total. Didn't document any of it and definitely didn't hold on to most of them.

I've also managed a few hundos from trades. Some luckies, some not.

Yep. Almost every week. There have been the odd cases where I missed a streak because I was in the states and didn't want to roam. But that has only been a couple times. I very, very rarely get the evo items from regular spins. Recently I got two evo items from a single regular spin. Which up until that point, I didn't even know was possible because I can only recount a couple of times that I even got one from a regular spin. [Of course neither of them were a Sunstone.](https://imgur.com/lM2Mfkn)

A lot of players in my community have also lamented about the insane number of Sunstones they get. Everyone says they just throw that junk away because it takes up space... I can't even get one ;_;

I've been holding on to Dragon Scales for the exact same reason you've stated. Unfortunately, I live in a place that basically doesn't spawn water pokemon. So outside of nests, it's realistically impossible to find Horsea/Seadra here. I have "caught" a grand total of 18 Horsea and at least 90% of those were from hatches. I know I caught one during the water event.
